# This repo is public, and it holds a proposal-writing tool rather than anybody's
# proposals. The rule: the project is pushed, the data is not. Guides, rules,
# templates, the server and the UI are the project and they all ship. Who the
# people are, what was written for whom, and the images that went with it are
# custom data, so they live in profiles/ and proposals/ and stay here. Somebody
# else can clone this and drop their own people in.
#
# Add to the patterns rather than naming single files: the one-file-at-a-time
# approach is how a confidential tender reached the public remote on 2026-10-09.

# The person profiles, and the documents they were built from. Real names,
# rates, client work and candid assessments written for our own use.
profiles/

# Per-job images and the HTML they were rendered from. They live in proposals/
# now, so they are already covered, but a stray one at the root is still caught.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
!ui/favicon.png
milestones-job.html
approach-job.html

# Job queue records: contain pasted job descriptions and drafted proposals
.jobs/

# Jobs pulled off the relay before they are written. Same content as .jobs,
# one step earlier.
.queue/

# Relay threads: the server's instructions to this worker and our replies.
# Ten of these were on the public remote before being ignored here.
.threads/

# Runtime state for the three workers: which are running, paused or stopped,
# and what each is on. A folder rather than a file, so the next bit of state
# has somewhere to go without anybody naming it in here one at a time.
.state/

# The local proposal archive. Kept out of the public repo because these carry
# client names, job descriptions and rates. Delete this line to version them.
proposals/

# Source documents that belong to other people. Clients send briefs, tenders
# and scoping documents as attachments, and they are confidential by default
# even when nothing says so. Never commit one; keep the pattern, not a list.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf
*.rtf
*.odt
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.pptx
*.rar
*.zip

# Relay worker credentials. This repo is public: the token must never be in it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
proposal-bridge.json

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
